    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That hits the nail on the head. It's exactly the kind of bluntness I'm looking for. \n\nOne last thing to tighten it up, though. I want to wrap up the speech with a really powerful closing. I want to call out the idea that \"voter apathy\" is just a personal choice or a character trait, and instead frame it as something that's actually damaging the very fabric of how we live together. \n\nCould you write a concluding paragraph that moves beyond just \"voting is good\" and really drives home that abstaining from the vote is a failure to fulfill our part in the social contract? I want it to feel like a heavy responsibility that we all carry.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
